/* char-weiss runtime: her glyphs (docs/cross-effect/weiss/KIT_DESIGN.md, version B "Constellation"), appended to
   gameplay/buff/BuffFuncs by bbmod. Her Cross Tag loop: a held Ice Shard leaves a glyph; a lunge or a dive that passes
   near a glyph opens her follow-ups, which chain while glyphs remain, each one using a glyph.

   rwiPlace (rwi_place, on her held-Skill cast): a glyph (her bullet rwib2, action rwi_glyph) at the spot the cast names
     (ground: 1.6 u ahead, 0.9 u up; air: 2.0 u ahead, 1.6 u up). Past her limit the oldest black glyph ends (rwi_glyph_end).
   No glyph of hers lands on another: one that would crowd one goes to the next slot of its row, 1.4 u on (slot).
   Two kinds (the lead, 2026-11-01 night): the held Skill's glyph is black and serves her actions; the tapped Skill's
   is white and fires on its own (rwiSentry), at Lambda's portal's pace.
   rwiShot (rwi_shot, on her tapped Skill): a white glyph (rwi_glyph_white) 1.6 u ahead, and nothing fired of its own
     (2026-11-02); it lives 10 s (whiteLife), past her limit the oldest white one ends.
   rwiSeek (rwi_seek, every 0.05 s through a lunge, a dive or a follow-up): her nearest black glyph within reach is
     marked and she gets rwi_lit for 0.5 s; the follow-up switches read that buff.
   rwiUse (rwi_use, as a glyph action starts): one of the marked glyph's USES is spent: it flashes white
     (rwi_glyph_flash) and fires a shard at the nearest enemy; the last use ends it.
   rwiEx (rwi_ex, on EX Ice Shard): two black glyphs behind the nearest enemy, outside the black glyphs' own limit.
   rwiPlaceShort (rwi_place_short, as a lunge that hit ends, with Lunge Glyph): a 2-second glyph there.
   rwiBurst (rwi_burst, as Snowfall lands, with Glyph Burst): the nearest glyph fires a ring of six shards and stays.
   rwiJumpGlyph (rwi_jump_glyph, as she double jumps, with Jump 2): a 2-second glyph under her.
   rwiWaves (rwi_waves, as Glacial Torrent's wave starts, with Glacial Torrent 2): an ice arrow with the pillar from each glyph.
   (0.4.7) At most MAX_OUT (3) of her glyphs are out at once, every colour and every card's counted (capOut); a
   waiting glyph draws smaller than when cast, without its glow plane (growTick).
   Every change to her glyphs also sets or clears rwi_three (three or more out), which White Night's switch reads.
   Her Ice Shard cards change these: Twin Shards (21307) two shards where one flew (a white glyph's shot included),
   Keen Ice (21308) the faster shard bullet (rwi_shard_sentry_fast for a white glyph's), Third Glyph (21310) three glyphs at once. Universal Enhancement 1 (21322) shards that break Strong armor,
   2 (21323) glyphs that last 20 s; Potential Unleashed (21325) one more glyph at once.
   Battle time only (no real time, no random): every player runs the same steps (docs/four-player/MULTIPLAYER_CHECK.md).
   Every step is guarded: a failure logs once (tag WEISS) and the game goes on. */
(function () {
  var U = Util_1.U, CS = csharp_1;
  var S = globalThis.RWI || (globalThis.RWI = { said: {}, lit: {}, born: {} });
  S.ex = S.ex || {}; S.uses = S.uses || {};
  var GLYPH_BULLET = 20130102, LIMIT = 2, REACH = 1.4, USES = 3, WHITE = "rwi_glyph_white";
  var TWIN = 21307, KEEN = 21308, THIRD = 21310, UNI1 = 21322, UNI2 = 21323, PU = 21325;
  // Dust as Ruby's (the lead, 2026-11-02): Summon and a direction equips one Dust (her rwi_dustsw_* actions call rwiDust
  // as it locks); every white glyph she makes comes out in it, Ice until she picks another. Each Dust card makes that
  // Dust's white glyphs fire every DUST_CARD_EVERY s instead of SENTRY_EVERY
  var FIRE = 21328, BOLT = 21329, WIND = 21330, ZAP_STEP = 0.7, DUST_CARD_EVERY = 1.4;
  var DUST_CARD = { fire: FIRE, bolt: BOLT, wind: WIND };
  S.dust = S.dust || {};
  var WHITES = { rwi_glyph_white: "ice", rwi_glyph_fire: "fire", rwi_glyph_bolt: "bolt", rwi_glyph_wind: "wind" };
  var DUST_GLYPH = { ice: WHITE, fire: "rwi_glyph_fire", bolt: "rwi_glyph_bolt", wind: "rwi_glyph_wind" };
  var DUST_SHOT = { ice: "rwi_shard_sentry", fire: "rwi_dust_fire", wind: "rwi_dust_wind" };
